    detailedAnswer: "A staging area (or landing zone) is an intermediate storage location in an ETL/ELT pipeline that temporarily holds raw data extracted from source systems before it is cleaned, transformed, and loaded into the target data warehouse or data mart. It serves as a buffer between source systems and the target environment, isolating the extraction process from transformation logic. This allows for: 1) Data validation and quality checks before processing, 2) Reprocessing of data if errors occur, 3) Decoupling of extraction and transformation processes, and 4) Maintaining an audit trail of raw data for troubleshooting. Staging areas typically retain data for a limited period (days to weeks) and often have a schema similar to the source systems. Data in staging areas is often called 'raw' or 'stage' data and is not yet conformed to the target model."
