    correctAnswer: "Vectorized query engine for faster SQL",
    explanation: "Photon is Databricks' vectorized query engine that provides significant performance improvements for SQL workloads.",
    detailedAnswer: "Photon in Databricks is a next-generation, vectorized query execution engine that is specifically optimized for SQL workloads and provides significant performance improvements over traditional query engines. It was developed by Databricks to address the performance requirements of modern data analytics workloads, particularly in the context of the Lakehouse architecture. Photon represents a major advancement in query execution technology by implementing a vectorized execution model rather than the traditional row-by-row (or tuple-at-a-time) processing model. In a vectorized execution model, operations are performed on batches of data (vectors) at once, rather than on individual rows. This approach leverages modern CPU architectures, particularly SIMD (Single Instruction Multiple Data) instructions, which can perform the same operation on multiple data elements simultaneously. This results in much better CPU utilization and significantly improved performance. Key features and capabilities of Photon include: vectorized execution which processes data in batches of 1024 elements at a time, enabling efficient use of CPU cache and SIMD instructions, native code generation which compiles SQL queries into highly optimized native machine code that runs directly on the CPU, rather than interpreting queries, just-in-time (JIT) compilation which generates optimized code at runtime based on the specific characteristics of the query and data, and adaptive query execution which dynamically optimizes query plans based on runtime statistics and conditions. Photon provides several important benefits for SQL workloads in Databricks: significantly faster query performance with improvements of 2x to 10x or more for many queries, especially for analytical queries that process large volumes of data, reduced resource consumption as queries execute faster and require fewer CPU cycles, improved cost efficiency by enabling users to process more data with fewer resources, and seamless integration with the Databricks SQL ecosystem, allowing users to take advantage of Photon without changing their queries or applications. Photon works with Delta Lake tables and other data formats supported by Databricks, and it automatically optimizes queries based on the data distribution, file formats, and query characteristics. It supports various SQL features including: complex joins, aggregations, window functions, and nested data types. Photon is particularly effective for: analytical queries that scan and process large volumes of data, complex multi-table joins, aggregations and group-by operations, and queries that involve sorting, filtering, and projection operations. The engine is designed to work seamlessly with other Databricks features including: Delta Lake for optimized storage and performance, Auto Loader for continuous data ingestion, and Unity Catalog for governance and security. Photon is available in Databricks SQL and can be enabled with minimal configuration, making it easy for users to take advantage of its performance benefits without changing their existing queries or workflows."
