    detailedAnswer: "The output block in Terraform is used to export values from the Terraform configuration that may be useful for other systems, other Terraform configurations, or for the user to see. Outputs are essentially return values for a Terraform module or the root module. Outputs can expose any value that is known within the Terraform configuration, including resource attributes, variables, local values, or computed values from expressions. Outputs are only shown when explicitly requested using the terraform output command. By default, all output values are shown, but you can filter to specific outputs by name. Outputs can be marked as sensitive (using the sensitive = true parameter) to prevent their values from being shown in the command-line output, which is useful for values that contain secrets or sensitive information. Outputs are often used to display connection strings, IP addresses, DNS names, or other important information after infrastructure has been provisioned. They are also crucial when using modules - a child module can expose outputs that can be accessed by the parent module using the module.<MODULE_NAME>.<OUTPUT_NAME> syntax."
